

#include <iostream>
#include <algorithm>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    int n,W;
    int p[20],w[20],dp[21][101]={0};

    // Input number of items
    cout<<"Enter number of items: ";
    cin>>n;

    // Input profit and weight of each item
    for(int i=1;i<=n;i++)
    {
        cout<<"Enter profit and weight: ";
        cin>>p[i]>>w[i];
    }

    // Input knapsack capacity
    cout<<"Enter capacity: ";
    cin>>W;

    // Fill DP table using Dynamic Programming
    for(int i=1;i<=n;i++)
    {
        for(int j=0;j<=W;j++)
        {
            // Check whether item can fit
            if(w[i]<=j)
                // Choose maximum profit: include or exclude item
                dp[i][j]=max(p[i]+dp[i-1][j-w[i]],
                             dp[i-1][j]);
            else
                // Exclude item if it does not fit
                dp[i][j]=dp[i-1][j];
        }
    }

    // Display maximum profit
    cout<<"Maximum Profit = "<<dp[n][W];

    return 0;
}





















































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































Start the program.

Take the number of items as input.

Take the profit and weight of each item.

Take the maximum capacity of the knapsack.

Create a 2D DP table and initialize all values to zero.

Consider each item one by one.

Check whether the current item's weight is less than or equal to the available capacity.

If the item fits, calculate two possibilities:
	- Include the item and add its profit.
	- Exclude the item and keep the previous profit.

Select the maximum profit from both possibilities.

If the item does not fit, exclude it.

Store the calculated maximum profit in the DP table.

Repeat this process for all items and capacities.

Finally, display the maximum profit from the DP table.

Stop the program.